#: ../../source/docs/ac2_followme.rst:5
#: 844825de1fef4a7cbdbfaf094aee963e
msgid "Follow Me Mode (GCS Enabled)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_followme.rst:7
#: 3e2356cc06a843bfaf70dae3e4ccb171
msgid "Follow Me mode makes it possible for you to have your copter follow you as you move, using a telemetry radio and a ground station."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_followme.rst:12
#: e387cf6ef5084bd483971436f75bda4c
msgid "Unlike other autopilot modes, this feature is implemented in the Ground Station. The ground station controls the movement by reading the vehicle position using MAVLink Telemetry and sending GUIDED mode instructions to move the vehicle appropriately. Currently this sort of functionality is supported by *Mission Planner* for Windows laptops, APM Planner for OS X laptops, and DroidPlanner for Android devices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_followme.rst:20
#: 54b1d7700c0e4374ae0a118e432366a0
msgid "What you'll need"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_followme.rst:22
#: 8b706440c40b4f958442d0d8cbcf4c3a
msgid "A Copter with telemetry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_followme.rst:23
#: 28e4da69268c4119bd07d61f8337a680
msgid "A laptop (or a phone/tablet with an integrated GPS available to the GCS app)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_followme.rst:24
#: 7ef80f503081433bb9de2e6e18994ee8
msgid "A GPS USB dongle `like this <https://www.amazon.com/ND-100S-GlobalSat-USB-GPS-Receiver/dp/B004K39QTY/>`__ or Bluetooth GPS module `like this <https://www.amazon.com/GlobalSat-BT-368i-Bluetooth-GPS-Receiver/dp/B0018YZ836/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_followme.rst:28
#: abbc53b20a8a47db81b2201b598be4b7
msgid "Instructions for Mission Planner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_followme.rst:30
#: e6489a9e48ec435b82a6c943d6e904a5
msgid "Set one of your flight modes to \"Loiter\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_followme.rst:31
#: 61e86da13a574be390502fbec81c11aa
msgid "Set up your Copter and establish a MAVLink connection over wireless telemetry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_followme.rst:33
#: f4221c65097744ae85e73bada600548c
msgid "Ensure that your GPS USB dongle or Bluetooth device is plugged into to your laptop and showing up as a serial port. Using the software that came with the module, make sure that it's working and that you have GPS lock."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_followme.rst:37
#: c3e02b7e26f84881895c6d60170ff45e
msgid "Take off, and once in the air switch to Loiter. (Make sure there's sufficient altitude to ensure the drone does not injure you)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_followme.rst:39
#: 7ead5d7138ce4c3f8f530cfa81849bcb
msgid "In Mission Planner Flight Data screen try right-clicking on a nearby spot and select \"Fly to Here\". If this works, you're ready to try Follow Me mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_followme.rst:42
#: 158289d1b65c43f3a96582a3b61d59bc
msgid "In Mission Planner, enter Control-F to open the following window. Click on \"Follow Me\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_followme.rst:48
#: 0539cd0f06ef4b888e5b1bcb6ec740d6
msgid "This will bring up this window. Select the serial port that's assigned to your GPS device and the baud rate it uses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_followme.rst:53
#: 22b0a2114f974b98b7552594c3ca2aa7
msgid "Once you click \"Connect\", Mission Planner will read GPS data from your device and send it to your Copter as \"fly to here\" commands every two seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_followme.rst:57
#: 559b4af1be924385ad22203e70658e80
msgid "Now pick up your laptop and start walking around."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_followme.rst:58
#: 514af5d9b49f4f269c72be28084f6e03
msgid "The Copter should follow you!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_followme.rst:60
#: ddf6d45c1f0d4791955f45968779bb46
msgid "Make sure to set sufficient altitude to prevent any injuries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_followme.rst:61
#: 5a7efb3f431a4d2ca5e8e79a68d524ab
msgid "If proper altitude is set, you can make it follow you and attempt to out run it!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ac2_followme.rst:65
#: 46f94a225246495ba8b9f086826910a6
msgid "The barometer is used in the altitude calculation meaning that it can drift over time and impact rising terrain. Watch for obstacles and elevation changes. The altitude maintaining behavior is similar to loiter mode."
msgstr ""
